<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-1.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-1.png" alt="" width="840" height="560" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-89442" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-1.png 1683w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-1-300x200.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-1-1024x683.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-1-768x512.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-1-1536x1024.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>What?  Already?  It seems like I was doing a posting like this just the other week&#8230;</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13.png" alt="" width="840" height="177" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-89439" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13.png 1233w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-300x63.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-1024x216.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-768x162.png 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>How time flies &#8212; it was three weeks ago.  But this was a speedy stretch, and we actually decreased the numbers of open bugs, from 2590 to 2466, which, if my mathematics knowledge is correct, is &#8230;  more than a hundred.  Approx.  Don&#8217;t take my word for it.</p>
<p>Oh, yeah, if you&#8217;re just joining the show, this is the blog post where I natter on a bit about Emacs development, through the lens of traversing the Emacs bug tracker.</p>
<p>To zoom out:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-2.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-2.png" alt="" width="840" height="570" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-89443" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-2.png 1603w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-2-300x204.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-2-1024x695.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-2-768x521.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-2-1536x1043.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>We&#8217;re on a downward trend, but I feel like it&#8217;s taking more effort recently.  I didn&#8217;t implement a single significant new feature this cycle, but just concentrated on triage and fixing (small) stuff, and it still was&#8230;  a lot of work.</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-3.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-3.png" alt="" width="840" height="554" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-89444" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-3.png 1653w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-3-300x198.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-3-1024x676.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-3-768x507.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-3-1536x1014.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>And it looks like the number of opened bugs is pretty flat?  Or&#8230;  is it?  So I made a <a href="https://quimby.gnus.org/circus/stats-emacs/stats-emacs.html" data-cached-time="2022-02-13T12:05:41" data-cached-image="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/ewptMT8YD.png" onmouseenter="hoverLink(event)">new chart</a>:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-4.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-4.png" alt="" width="840" height="561" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-89445" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-4.png 1615w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-4-300x200.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-4-1024x684.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-4-768x513.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-4-1536x1026.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Aha!  The number of bugs opened per month was in the 150 region from 2015 to 2020, but the last couple years, we&#8217;ve trended towards 200 per month.  Which says something, but I&#8217;m not sure what.</p>
<p>How do you interpret a higher bug count?  Is Emacs getting buggier, or are we just adding more new stuff (that then has bugs (everything does)), or is the number of users increasing, so we&#8217;re getting more reports?  Difficult to say, but I think it&#8217;s mostly the second point.  To take just one example (but a big one) &#8212; the pure Gtk branch was merged a couple months ago, and that led to a surge in bug reports from users trying that out.</p>
<p>Let&#8217;s see&#8230;  did Emacs get anything new and exciting since the last blog post?  Uhm&#8230;  Oh, yeah:</p>
<p><a class=cimage href="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-5.png"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-5.png" alt="" width="840" height="430" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-89446" srcset="https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-5.png 1722w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-5-300x154.png 300w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-5-1024x525.png 1024w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-5-768x394.png 768w, https://lars.ingebrigtsen.no/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/2022-02-13-5-1536x788.png 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></a></p>
<p>Emacs can now (courtesy of Håkon Flatval and Po Lu) use alpha backgrounds (i.e., let windows behind Emacs frames shine through).</p>
<p>In total, there&#8217;s been 610 commits, for an average of 28 per day.  Ish.</p>
<p>Next stretch is just 246 bugs, but I think I&#8217;ll be concentrating on implementing things instead of looking at old bug reports, so it&#8217;ll probably take a whole lot longer until the next blog post in this series.</p>
<p>And I may be taking some time off, but whenever I say that, it never happens.</p>
